  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post-arrival Humanitarian Assistance and Protection Support for Afghan Returnees from Pakistan and Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan is facing an unprecedented humanitarian crisis with a very real risk of systemic collapse and human catastrophe. This humanitarian crisis is reversing many of the gains of the last 20 years, including around women&#x2019;s rights.  At the end of 2023, returnees from Islamic republic of Iran and Pakistan arrived in Afghanistan through different border crossings and the trend is expected to increase through 2024. Through this project, IOM addresses the humanitarian needs of vulnerable undocumented Afghan migrants returning from Islamic republic of Iran and Pakistan through operations at the reception centers, on the border with Islamic republic of Iran and Pakistan and their respective transit centers, and in the provinces of return.</narrative>
  </description>
